ATTEMPT-2 FIX VERIFICATION (the settled item 8 defect):

- type:"transfer" now works: TestSearchTransactionsFiltersByTypeTransfer
  passes — returns 1 row, Type="Transfer", Amount=-3000, SumAmount=-3000.
  Against the pre-fix code (search.go reverted via `git stash` in a scratch
  copy OUTSIDE the repo) this test FAILS: "type \"transfer\" must be a valid
  filter, not an error" (the old switch's default branch returned "not
  recognized").

- Default path: sum_amount EXCLUDES transfers while `total` and the listed
  rows STILL INCLUDE them. TestSearchTransactionsDefaultSumExcludesTransfers:
  out.Total==3 (transfer listed), out.SumAmount==3800 (Income 5000 + Outflow
  -1200, NOT 800 which would net the -3000 transfer). A probe test
  (zz_page_check_test.go, since removed) confirmed the page rows include a
  Type="Transfer", Amount=-3000 row on the default path. Both halves hold:
  listing keeps transfers, sum excludes them. Against the pre-fix code this
  test FAILS: "sum_amount = 800 matches the NETTED-IN transfer total".

- sum_amount agrees with summarize_spending's net_savings for the same
  fixture. A probe test (zz_crosscheck_test.go, since removed) drove both
  tools over searchFixtureWithTransfer(): net_savings=3800, sum_amount=3800.
  They agree because metrics.Calculate computes
  netSavings = totalIncome - |sum outflows| = 5000 - 1200 = 3800, and
  search's default sum is Income.SumAmount() + Outflow.SumAmount() =
  5000 + (-1200) = 3800.

- The new tests fail against the pre-fix code. Confirmed by copying the
  worktree to /tmp/a9_prefix_check, reverting spend/search.go via
  `git stash`, and re-running: both new tests FAIL (sum=800 netted-in;
  transfer rejected as "not recognized"). Restored afterward.

- The descriptions are TRUE of the code as it now stands. search.go:95-100
  describes "on the default path (no type filter) it EXCLUDES Transfer rows
  even though they are still listed (`total` and the page include them)...
  with an explicit type filter the filtered set is already one type, so the
  exclusion only matters on the default path" — matches behavior
  (default: Income+Outflow sum; explicit: full filtered sum, including
  transfer). server.go:94-101 "excluded from both totals by type filter...
  rows REMAIN in the ledger and are visible through get_transfers... spending
  tools therefore do NOT COUNT savings or investment contributions in their
  totals" — TRUE: metrics.Calculate and the search default both exclude
  transfers from totals, get_transfers lists them. This is NOT the
  inverse-of-behavior shape A1 attempt 3 exhibited; the text now matches the
  code.

